# CampusFlow learning resources — manual REST Client flows (faculty/admin).
@base = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@subjectId = <subject-id>

### Login as faculty
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "faculty@institution.edu",
  "password": "Faculty@123"
}

### Create resource with PDF attachment (multipart)
POST {{base}}/study/learning-resources
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="subject"

{{subjectId}}
--cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="topic"

Week 4 revision
--cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Lecture notes
--cf-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./notes.pdf
--cf-boundary--

### Create resource with external link (JSON)
POST {{base}}/study/learning-resources
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "{{subjectId}}",
  "topic": "Week 4 revision",
  "title": "Reference article",
  "url": "https://example.com/article",
  "type": "link",
  "difficulty": "beginner"
}

### List resources
GET {{base}}/study/learning-resources?subject={{subjectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
